  "body": "## What this PR does\nThis PR is the release branch of CamCraft 0.28.0. It merges into `main` after the cut gate is green and after an independent review.\n\n- `RECOMMENDED.md` gets the 155 decision files of the cut under one `v0.28.0` heading. The files are removed from `docs/decisions/`.\n- `RELEASE_NOTES.md` has the 0.28.0 notes: breaking changes, upgrade notes, changes to posted G-code, highlights, known issues and process changes.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` has one 0.28.0 row for each behaviour PR merged since v0.27.0.\n- `cargo xtask release --version 0.28.0 --no-tag --skip-gate` set the version to 0.28.0 in `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock`.\n\n## Cut list\nThe cut line is 2026-11-27T20:59Z (the maintainer's answers in the question dialog).\n\nIn the cut:\n- #4133 / PR #4440: the site tests in the gate. Merged as d5544b6f5.\n- #4341: the Z retract before a tool change. PR #4509 supersedes PR #4371. Merged as 740b44133 on 2026-11-28.\n- #4431 / PR #4405: the red `main` (the two `wire_post` tests write into a temp folder). Merged.\n- Always in a cut: a fix for a red `main` or a red cut gate.\n\nThe maintainer added these PRs after the cut line (\"Include them, then freeze\"; \"yeah include both\"):\n- #4410, #4449, #4423, #4424, #4368, #4441 and #4438.\n\nThese seven PRs merged into `main` after the freeze notice, between 00:01Z and 00:02Z on 2026-11-28. They stay in the release, and the release notes name them:\n- #4467, #4298, #4442, #4425, #4458, #4459 and #4460.\n\nOut by decision: #4312, and #4383 (kernel to `main`, merges after the tag).\n\nNo other PR merged into `main` after 2394b5ad1 except PR #4509.\n\n## Known issues\nEach open `P1` and `P2` issue that is not on the cut list is in the \"Known issues\" section of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. A comment on this PR lists them.\n\n## What did not run\n- No Windows machine: the pixel-snapshot lanes and the Windows per-OS readings did not run.\n- The cut gate has not run: no online cut runner has zola and node.\n- The local package step of `cargo xtask release` stopped at phase 8 (`package-linux: missing rpmbuild`). The release build and the post version check (0.28.0) passed. `release.yml` builds the published packages from the tag.\n\nChangelog: none (release mechanics)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
